    skos:exactMatch <https://openalex.org/T11214> ;
    skos:scopeNote "This cluster of papers focuses on genetic and behavioral studies related to the domestication of dogs, including genomic analysis, animal-assisted therapy, social cognition, human-animal bond, genetic structure, oxytocin, behavioral traits, canine genetics, and an evolutionary view of domestication. The papers cover a wide range of topics such as the origin of domestic dogs, genetic evidence for dog domestication, the impact of pets on human health and psychological well-being, and the cognitive evolution in captive foxes as a correlated by-product of experimental domestication."@en ;
    caveat:openAlexKeyword "Animal-Assisted Therapy"@en, "Behavioral Traits"@en, "Canine Genetics"@en, "Dog Domestication"@en, "Evolutionary View"@en, "Genetic Structure"@en, "Genomic Analysis"@en, "Human-Animal Bond"@en, "Oxytocin"@en, "Social Cognition"@en ;
